[-68.15,-15.99,11,5]},{"tree":[78.31,23.16,11,5]},{"tree":[83.05,-51.02,11,5]},{"tree":[27.42,-45.48,11,5]},{"mesh":{"v":[-87.31,62.32,0,-29.63,45.79,0,-25.77,59.24,0,-83.45,75.78,0,-87.31,62.32,0.5,-29.63,45.79,0.5,-25.77,59.24,0.5,-83.45,75.78,0.5],"f":[0,2,1,0,3,2,4,5,6,4,6,7,0,1,5,0,5,4,1,2,6,1,6,5,2,3,7,2,7,6,3,0,4,3,4,7]},"m":"gravel"}],"notes":"Parrish Art Museum, Water Mill (Herzog and de Meuron, 2012): a single long building, about 187 m by 29 m, under twin barn-like gabled roofs of corrugated galvanised metal that overhang the white-painted concrete walls to make porches down both long sides, with slim posts; long stretches of glass at the entrance, café and studios, skylights along the north slopes; set in a meadow. Turned 16 degrees north of east to lie along its axis in the ground file. Written from general knowledge; guessed: eave and ridge heights (about 5 and 10 m), the skylight rhythm, where the glass runs. No photographs were available."}